# The three calls of a conversion to a primitive are left once for each value, at the first converting operation in the order of the blocks. `if (turns === limit) break;` numbers the code behind the loop in front of the rest of the turn, so that operation is the one behind the loop. The summary keeps the site in the loop too, and whoever follows the start of the program enters `toString` there: in front of the store that lays `read`, which is therefore not laid ahead of every object.
